  <static seed="1885" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionSubtractionWordProblems50.pg">
    <statement><p>Carl and Brent are sharing a pizza. Carl ate <m>{{\frac{2}{9}}}</m> of the pizza, and Brent ate <m>{{\frac{1}{10}}}</m> of the pizza. How much more pizza did Carl eat than Brent?</p>
<p>Carl ate <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> more of the pizza than Brent ate.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{11}{90}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To find the difference of two numbers, we use subtraction:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{2}{9}}} - {{\frac{1}{10}}} 
      \amp = \frac{2 \cdot 10}{9 \cdot 10}-\frac{1 \cdot 9}{10 \cdot 9} \\
      \amp = \frac{20}{90} - \frac{9}{90} \\
      \amp = \frac{20-9}{90} \\
      
      \amp = {{\frac{11}{90}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Carl ate <m>{{\frac{11}{90}}}</m> more of the pizza than Brent ate.</p>
</solution>
